    "type": "Manifest",
    "label": {
        "en": ["Overlapping composite canvas renderer fixture"]
    },
    "summary": {
        "en": [
            "One canvas painted by a full-canvas image with a SMALLER image inset over the middle of it — IIIF Cookbook recipe 0036's real shape, where a miniature sits on top of the folio it belongs to. The sibling `composite` fixture places its two images side by side, which is what makes their placement checkable; this one places them ON each other, which is what makes their PAINT ORDER checkable. Both are the same numbered grid, so the inset maps the whole grid into a third of the canvas and its markers land where the full-canvas image has only background — a point that shows the inset's red marker if and only if the inset painted last. The inset is small enough to settle on a coarser pyramid level than the image beneath it, which is the condition under which a draw list sorted globally by level paints the big image over the small one."
        ]
    },
